{"name":"New Love","hex":"#c6bbdb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"new","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Newar."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Recently made, or created.","Of recent origin; having taken place recently."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/new"},{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"}],"entries":[{"title":"New Love","blocks":[{"text":"\"New Love\" is the debut single by English singer Dua Lipa from her eponymous debut studio album (2017). It was written by Lipa and its producers Emile Haynie and Andrew Wyatt about the singer's struggle to find her place in the music industry. The song is a synth-pop ballad with neo soul and R&B elements as well as a stomping, tribal drum beat throughout. Several music critics complimented the song's showcase of Lipa's vocals."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/20/Dua_Lipa_-_New_Love.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Love","wikidata":"Q89279789"},{"title":"New Love (Silk City song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"New Love\" is a song by British-American superduo Silk City, featuring vocals from English singer Ellie Goulding. It was released as a digital download and for streaming on 21 January 2021. The song was written by Clément Picard, Ellie Goulding, Mark Ronson, Maxime Picard, Steve McCutcheon and Thomas Wesley Pentz."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1b/Silk_City_-_New_Love.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Love_(Silk_City_song)","wikidata":"Q105015879"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love","wikidata":"Q316"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/5c/Dua_Lipa_-_New_Love_music_video.png/330px-Dua_Lipa_-_New_Love_music_video.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/5c/Dua_Lipa_-_New_Love_music_video.png/330px-Dua_Lipa_-_New_Love_music_video.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A scene from the Super 8 film format music video that makes heavy use of colour and effect filters in the style of psychedelic art","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADua_Lipa_-_New_Love_music_video.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg/500px-Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg/1280px-Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg/500px-Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fraternal love (Prehispanic sculpture from 250 to 900 CE, of Huastec origin). Museum of Anthropology in Xalapa, Veracruz, Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColumpio_Veracruz_059.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wi